      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "An example would be trying to use the debug menu to check logs while debugging a vehicle, or specifically like with NeoWorlds where the player may move large distances for what is perceivably normal movement in a secondary game world.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-11-11T01:27:47.568Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The entire Debug Menu canvas should have a setting for changing the tracking space it resides in: Head, Playspace, World. This should act the exact same (or as close as possible) to the Personal Mirror Tracking options. The Personal Mirror is a great example of how it would be expected to act: Following Head, Locally attached to player, or plainly in the World (default).\n\nDoing this would allow creators to keep the menu in view while traveling in a station, between teleporting, and anything involving movement to keep the logs in view.\n\nThis setting should be accessible outside of the Debug Menu canvas (like in the big menu or in a radial menu like Personal Mirror) so that tracking space can be returned if the Debug Menu canvas is inaccessible.",
